<title>FRANCE: Strauss-Kahn says no need to reassure Germany.</title>
<headline>Strauss-Kahn says no need to reassure Germany.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn said on Thursday Germany should not be worried by the change of government in France.</p>
<p>Asked by a German television reporter if he had anything to say to Germany, Strauss-Kahn said:</p>
<p>&quot;There is no reason for Germany to be worried, so there is no reason for me to reassure them.&quot;</p>
<p>He was speaking to reporters after the handover of power between outgoing Finance Minister Jean Arthuis and Strauss-Kahn.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
